  "_comment": "DOCKING CANDIDATE (bellows): the heavy hard-dock. A wide armour ring fills the -Z cell face, four corner clamps stand around it, and the sleeve telescopes in TWO stages - a 0.345..0.365 root barrel and a 0.30..0.315 outer barrel - so the extended tube wears a visible shoulder instead of one clean cone. The profile still rises monotonically from the mouth, which is what lets two facing ports nest; the shoulder gives the overlap a second, wider contact the plain taper has not got. Costs a second sleeve and a heavier face. Nothing keys, nothing decorates the mouth: the clamps and hazard bands live on the cell body.",
